      "customfield_10012" : "0|i00293:",
      "customfield_10300" : "{}",
      "description" : {
         "content" : [
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "•\tDocument design choice with Stroika iterator.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "o\tCopy versus Reference",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "\tIn Java, they make the choice to reference, and then throw exception when they detect conflict – container change while iterating (check count flag)",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "\tCopying intrinsicly more costly for large objects, but this is often optimizable away (mostly) for pod (e.g. int/pointer) types) .",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "\tThen only cost one we have anyhow – of one virutla  function per NEXT call, and after that very checap and no locking",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "\tAnd inside virtual REP impl – there we can do the java-style trick of looking at lock counts, but instead of throwing – we smartly retry (or for simplicity just always use locking –up to impl).",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            }
         ],
         "type" : "doc",
         "version" : 1
      },
